  1376.1 ? dial=c7  "[p.54:] 3. Indicate the answers to the questions as follows: If the answer to question A is YES, move slide switch 4 to the LEFT. If the answer to question A is NO, move slide switch 4 to the RIGHT. If the answer to question B is YES, move slide switch 5 to the LEFT. If the answer to question B is NO, move slide switch 5 to the RIGHT. If the answer to question C is YES, move slide switch 6 to the LEFT. If the answer to question C is NO, move slide switch 6 to the RIGHT. 4. Push pushbutton 6. The pointer knob of the rotary switch will turn to the number your friend was thinking of. [p.51:] A) Is Number Greater Than 3? / Yes (Number is) (4, 5, 6 or 7) / B) Is Remainder Greater Than 1? / Yes (Number is) ( 6 or 7 ) / C) Is Number Odd? / Yes (Number) ( is 7 ) [Book I p.20:] For example, when the pointer knob points at 1, the wiper arm makes an electrical connection between D1 and D16."
  9376.1 ? dial=c7  "[p.54:] 3. Indicate the answers to the questions as follows: If the answer to question A is YES, move slide switch 4 to the LEFT. If the answer to question A is NO, move slide switch 4 to the RIGHT. If the answer to question B is YES, move slide switch 5 to the LEFT. If the answer to question B is NO, move slide switch 5 to the RIGHT. If the answer to question C is YES, move slide switch 6 to the LEFT. If the answer to question C is NO, move slide switch 6 to the RIGHT. 4. Push pushbutton 6. The pointer knob of the rotary switch will turn to the number your friend was thinking of. [p.51:] A) Is Number Greater Than 3? / Yes (Number is) (4, 5, 6 or 7) / B) Is Remainder Greater Than 1? / Yes (Number is) ( 6 or 7 ) / C) Is Number Odd? / Yes (Number) ( is 7 ) [Book I p.20:] For example, when the pointer knob points at 1, the wiper arm makes an electrical connection between D1 and D16."
